NAME
    kill - send a signal to a process

SYNOPSIS
    kill PID [PID...]
    kill -SIG PID [PID...]

DESCRIPTION
    Sends SIG (default: SIGTERM) to each PID. SIG may be a number
    (e.g. -9) or a name (e.g. -KILL). Supported signals:

      1   HUP     hang-up
      2   INT     interrupt (Ctrl-C from a terminal)
      9   KILL    uncatchable terminate
      15  TERM    terminate (default)
      17  CHLD    child exited
      18  CONT    continue (resume a stopped task)
      19  STOP    uncatchable stop
      20  TSTP    stop from terminal (Ctrl-Z)

    KILL and STOP cannot be caught or blocked. Everything else can
    be installed via sys_sigaction (libuser's sig_install wrapper).

EXAMPLES
    kill 17                             # SIGTERM the task at pid 17
    kill -9 17                          # SIGKILL the task at pid 17
    kill -STOP 12                       # pause pid 12
    kill -CONT 12                       # resume it

EXIT STATUS
    0   every signal was delivered
    1   at least one PID was missing or not signalable

SEE ALSO
    ps(1), signal(2)
